I DEARLY beloved brethren, the Scripture
  moveth us in sundry places to acknowledge
  and confess our manifold sins and wickedness; and
  that we should not dissemble nor cloke them before
  the face of Almighty God our heavenly Father;
  but confess them with an humble, lowly, peni-
  tent, and obedient heart; to the end that we may
  obtain forgiveness of the same, by his infinite
  goodness and mercy. And although we ought
